TEST T12067 -- Flow control operation with MDI -- tb470 IE520 stack -- 2026-10-02 -- UNSUPPORTED
==================================================================================================

VERDICT: UNSUPPORTED. The case tests 802.3x flow control under each MDI configuration. The IE520
supports neither half of it on this build (awplus_main-20260923-20):
  1. FLOW CONTROL: the DUT REFUSES to enable it, on every port tried, on both IE520s, and its own log
     says why: "DBG:exfx_port_flowControlSet 1979: Configuring flow-control receive is not supported
     on this product". With flow control unset, it ignores received PAUSE frames (measured, B1).
  2. MDI/MDI-X (steps 2 and 3): every front port is an SFP cage, and polarity is UNSUPPORTED here
     (bench owner's ruling 2026-09-29, T33234; orient-dt §2). Both test ports read
     "current polarity auto". Steps 2-3 were not attempted.
Run label: clean (the bench delivered everything the case needs: wire-rate load, a separate PAUSE
source, and observation of PAUSE on the DUT and the hosts; it was the DUT that refused).
Note for the Test Engineer: the command PARSES (`flowcontrol {both|receive|send}`, `{on|off}`), then
fails with "% Error setting flow control ...". If the IE520 is meant to support 802.3x, this is a
defect rather than a platform gap and the grade should become FAIL. The platform's own message says
"not supported on this product", so it is graded UNSUPPORTED here.

Case text (ck.db AWPTCM-T12067, /Pause Control / Flow Control/.../Back Pressure/End to End test):
  objective: "Confirm that flowcontrol works correctly on all of supported MDI configuration."
  precondition: Tools IXIA*2; Set up IXIA1---DUT---IXIA2; "Set IXIA1,2 enable flow control send/receive."
  step 1: wire rate from IXIA1, then PAUSE from IXIA2 -> expect IXIA2 receives at 1/2 rate, and the DUT
          sends PAUSE to IXIA1 to suppress the original rate.
  step 2: same, after `polarity mdi` on the ports connected to IXIA1/2.
  step 3: same, after `polarity mdix`.
(The precondition's "see attachment cfg file" is not in ck.db: attachments NULL.)

