Relayed answer: "Proceed with both (Recommended)" -- T12067 by hand, step 1 measured, steps 2-3 UNSUPPORTED.

## Bench mapping
| case role | bench | DUT port | module |
| IXIA1 (load source, PAUSE observer) | tb470 eth1 (igc, 00:f0:4d:00:77:16) | stack port3.0.10 (member 3) | AT-SPTXc 1000BASE-T, a-full a-1000 |
| IXIA2 (receiver, PAUSE source)      | tb470 eth3 (igc, 00:f0:4d:00:77:18) | stack port3.0.9 (member 3)  | AT-SP10TM 10GBASE-TM at a-1000 |
| DUT | IE520 stack, master member 3, console /dev/u5 | | |
Both ports on one member: the case is a single-device IXIA1-DUT-IXIA2 path, so no stack link is in it.
Load: `tcpreplay -i eth1 --topspeed --duration=10 --loop=0` of 500 x 1000-byte frames, unicast to eth3's
MAC, ethertype 0x88B5 (no IP; never routed). PAUSE: scapy L2 socket on eth3, 01:80:c2:00:00:01 / 0x8808 /
opcode 0x0001 / quanta 0xFFFF (33.6 ms at 1 Gb/s), every 67 ms = ~50% duty, 13 s spanning the load window.
Observation: DUT `show platform port portX counters` (Pkts, FlowCtrlFrms RX/TX, Drop Events); host
`ethtool -S` (rx/tx_packets, rx/tx_flow_control_xon/xoff, rx_missed_errors). Tools: evidence/12067/.

## Pre-case
- Gate: precheck CLEAR; probe 2026-10-01T182835Z MATCH (the T24032 restore probe); boot configs
  flash:/tb470-bench.cfg on all four; running-configs = post-test-configs/2026-10-02-24032/.
- DUT: `show flowcontrol interface port3.0.9` / `port3.0.10` -> "Flow control is not set on interface ..."
- DUT counters (reset by the T24032 power cycles): FlowCtrlFrms 0/0 on both ports.
- Host: `ethtool -a eth1|eth3` -> Autonegotiate on, RX on, TX off (left unchanged throughout).

## B0 -- feature-off baseline: flow control unset, no PAUSE (07:31:20)
tcpreplay: "Actual: 1220501 packets (1220501000 bytes) sent in 10.00 seconds / Rated: ... 976.10 Mbps,
122013.49 pps" (wire rate for 1000-byte frames: 1000/1020 x 1 Gb/s = 980 Mb/s).
eth3 rx_packets +1220502 (all of them, +1 background); rx_missed_errors 0; all xon/xoff 0.
DUT: port3.0.10 RX Pkts 18 -> 1220519; port3.0.9 TX Pkts 908 -> 1221451; FlowCtrlFrms 0 everywhere; Drop Events 0.

## B1 -- PAUSE from IXIA2 with flow control unset (07:31:57)
"PAUSE sent: 195 frames on eth3 in 13.09 s, period 67.0 ms, quanta 0xffff, len 60"; eth3 tx_packets +195.
DUT port3.0.9 RX FlowCtrlFrms 0 -> 195: the PAUSE frames reached the DUT's MAC. This disproves the two
triage risks: igc does transmit software-built MAC-control frames, and the AT-SP10TM does not absorb them.
eth3 still received rx_packets +1220527 = the whole load (+26 background). tcpreplay again 976.10 Mbps.
=> With flow control unset, the DUT ignores PAUSE (expected for the feature-off state).

## Step 1 -- enable flow control on the DUT: REFUSED (07:3x)
  IE520-stk(config)#interface port3.0.9,port3.0.10
  IE520-stk(config-if)#flowcontrol receive on
  % Error setting flow control receive on port3.0.9
  % Error setting flow control receive on port3.0.10
  IE520-stk(config-if)#flowcontrol send on
  % Error setting flow control send on port3.0.9
  % Error setting flow control send on port3.0.10
  show flowcontrol interface port3.0.9  -> Flow control is not set on interface port3.0.9
  show flowcontrol interface port3.0.10 -> Flow control is not set on interface port3.0.10
  running-config: no flowcontrol line. Links stayed up (a-full a-1000).
The command exists (read-only help, sent without a CR and erased with Ctrl-U, in interface mode on port3.0.10):
  flowcontrol ?          -> both / receive / send
  flowcontrol receive ?  -> off / on
  flowcontrol send ?     -> off / on
The DUT's own log (show log | include flowCo):
  2026 Oct 01 18:33:26 local7.err IE520-stk EXFX[665]: DBG:exfx_port_flowControlSet 1979: Configuring flow-control receive is not supported on this product
  2026 Oct 01 18:33:27 local7.err IE520-stk EXFX[341]: Last message 'DBG:exfx_port_flowCo' repeated 1 times, suppressed by syslog-ng on IE520-stk
Not tied to the port or module:
  - stack port3.0.11 (empty cage, "not present"): the same two "% Error setting flow control ..." lines;
    log 18:34:38 the same "not supported on this product".
  - IE520-sa (standalone, /dev/u3, same build) port1.0.1 (empty cage): the same two errors;
    log 2026 Oct 01 18:35:23 local7.err IE520-sa EXFX[689]: DBG:exfx_port_flowControlSet 1979:
    Configuring flow-control receive is not supported on this product.
  Nothing was applied on any of them (show flowcontrol "not set"; running-config unchanged).
So the step-1 configuration ("enable flow control send/receive") cannot be set. Measuring the "1/2 rate"
and "DUT sends PAUSE to IXIA1" without it would only repeat B1. Not run.

## Steps 2 and 3 -- UNSUPPORTED (polarity on an SFP cage), not attempted
`show interface port3.0.10` / `port3.0.9`: "current duplex full, current speed 1000, current polarity auto /
configured ... polarity auto". Per the 2026-09-29 ruling (T33234), a DUT-side MDI/MDI-X role cannot
be set or resolved on these cages. They also depend on step 1's flow control, which is refused.

